{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1533 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "62443a81040899486e8d7d1994f0f100bc00419772ae0fcff6bed4450b1388a5" :edb/db-before-t 1532 :edb/db-after-t 1533 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534845 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:00:39.964Z" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186133719 1074 "The least-squares solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\nA^T A\\mathbf{x} = A^T\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, it satisfies $Q^T Q = I,$ and we get\n\n$$\nR^T R \\mathbf{x} = R^T \\! Q^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R^T$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $(R^T)^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ \\,R\\,\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $R$ and $Q^T.$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 false] [17592186133719 1074 "The least-squares solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\nA^T A\\mathbf{x} = A^T\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, it satisfies $Q^T Q = I,$ and we get\n\n$$\nR^T R \\mathbf{x} = R^T \\! Q^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R^T$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $(R^T)^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ \\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\,R\\phantom{|}}\\,\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $R$ and $Q^T.$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186133906 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440840 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186363391 1