{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $x$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 false] [17592186401097 1071 "$$\nx=\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186401097 1071 "$$\nx=\\boxed{}\\,\\boxed{}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139534845 17592186045417 false] [17592186401097 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & =\\,\\,\\,{R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 false] [17592186401097 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & =\\bbox[6px,border: 1px solid black]{\\,\\phantom{|}\\,\\,{R}^{-1}\\,}\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440834 1080 "$A$ and $b$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440834 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440834 1083 #uuid "29c6894b-ca73-55e4-b9e5-4515a24ac505" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440835 1080 "$m\\cdot {Q}^{-1}$ and $b$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440835 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440835 1083 #uuid "2b99f2e8-4b05-5e94-b564-250f2853615a" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440836 1080 "$b$ and $Q$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440836 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440836 1083 #uuid "4dd231d7-89bb-5f54-b089-0db260de5eac" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440837 1080 "${Q}^{T}$ and $b$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440837 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440837 1083 #uuid "eef0bb49-3a2a-51f2-9a63-905441460146" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [17592186440838 1080 "$Q$ and $b$" 13194139534845 17592186045417 true] [175921